ria-autocomplete="list" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="player-search-results" autoComplete="off" placeholder="Search players" class="h-9 w-full rounded-sm border border-border-strong bg-page pl-9 pr-3 text-sm text-ink outline-none placeholder:text-ink-muted focus:border-pitch-ink focus:ring-1 focus:ring-pitch-ink" value=""/></div></div><button type="button" aria-label="Theme: system (click to change)" title="Theme: system" class="flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-md border border-border text-ink-muted transition hover:text-ink"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" class="size-4" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="4" width="14" height="10" rx="1.5"></rect><path d="M7.5 17h5M10 14v3" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg></button><a class="text-xs font-semibold whitespace-nowrap text-pitch-ink hover:text-pitch-light" href="/pro?from=header">Get Pro</a><div class="h-8 w-24 animate-pulse rounded-sm bg-surface"></div></div><aside aria-label="FPL Planner" class="planner-banner flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-pitch-ink/30 bg-pitch/10 px-4 py-2 text-sm"><a class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 items-center gap-2 text-ink hover:text-pitch-ink" href="/fpl-planner"><span class="truncate"><strong class="font-semibold">Free FPL Planner<span class="hidden sm:inline">:</span></strong><span class="hidden sm:inline"> transfers, captain and chips for the next six gameweeks, with the FPL Cat model&#x27;s points.</span><span class="hidden min-[400px]:inline sm:hidden"> · next 6 GWs</span></span><span class="shrink-0 font-semibold text-pitch-ink">Plan my team →</span></a><button type="button" aria-label="Hide the planner banner for a week" class="shrink-0 rounded-full p-1 text-ink-muted hover:text-ink">✕</button></aside><main class="flex-1"><div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://fplcat.com"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Blog","item":"https://fplcat.com/blog"}]}</script><div class="relative overflow-hidden bg-pitch-dark"><svg class="pointer-events-none absolute top-1/2 -right-20 hidden h-96 w-96 -translate-y-1/2 text-white/10 sm:block" viewBox="0 0 200 200" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="100" cy="100" r="70" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"></circle><line x1="100" y1="0" x2="100" y2="200" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"></line></svg><div class="relative mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:py-12"><p class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-pitch-light">Blog</p><h1 class="mt-1 font-display text-4xl font-bold text-white sm:text-5xl">Fantasy Premier League strategy, explained</h1></div></div><div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12"><div class="divide-y divide-border border-y border-border"><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/thierno-barry-fpl-should-you-buy"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">7 November 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">Thierno Barry in FPL: He Finally Converted. Can He Do It Against Better Teams?</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">Two weeks ago Thierno Barry was missing chance after chance. Then came the winner at Newcastle and a 16-point haul against Coventry. With Brentford and Liverpool next, can Everton&#x27;s striker keep scoring against tougher defences?</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/fpl-ai-assistants-compared"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">5 November 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">FPL AI Assistants Compared 2026/27: 5 Tools, One Team, the Same 4 Questions</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">We asked FPL Cat, FPL Copilot, the official FPL Companion, ChatFPL.ai and Fantasy Football Fix&#x27;s ChatFPL the same four questions about one team in GW10. What they got right, what each costs, and what each is best for.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/fpl-differentials-gw10-14"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">3 November 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">5 FPL Differentials for the Next 5 Gameweeks</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">Five Fantasy Premier League players in fewer than 1 in 10 teams that I rate for Gameweeks 10 to 14, from a 1% midfielder to a defender who has kept six clean sheets in nine.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/dogeri-fpl-number-one-road-to-top"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">1 November 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">How ĐOGERI Reached FPL Number One: The Road to 735 Points</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">From 279,827th to first: ĐOGERI&#x27;s weekly scores, transfers, four chips and GW9 Wildcard squad, with a three-point lead while the gameweek remains open.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/elite-squads-gameweek-9-transfers-captains"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">31 October 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">Elite Squads Before Gameweek 9: Top Transfers and Captains</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">What the top 1,000 FPL managers did for GW9: João Pedro out, Nicolas Jackson in, Haaland captained by 93.3%, plus the top two managers&#x27; actual squads.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/biggest-fpl-flops-so-far-2026-27"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">29 October 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">FPL&#x27;s Biggest Flops So Far: 5 Pre-Season Favourites That Haven&#x27;t Clicked</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">Szoboszlai, Bruno Fernandes, Tzolis, Luke Shaw and O&#x27;Reilly were in almost every draft before GW1. Eight gameweeks in, I look at what went wrong.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/under-owned-fpl-picks-gw8-13"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">20 October 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">5 FPL Differentials for the Next 6 Gameweeks</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">Five Fantasy Premier League players almost nobody owns that I rate for the next six gameweeks, from a cut-price penalty taker to a defender in under 1% of teams.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/fpl-planner-apps-compared"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">18 October 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">Best FPL Planners 2026/27: Free &amp; Paid Apps Compared</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">Compare fpl.team, FPL Cat, PlanFPL, nextXI, LiveFPL, FPL Review and other FPL tools: planning features, free access and what to check before subscribing.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/manchester-united-fpl-players-to-buy-and-avoid"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">15 October 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">Manchester United: Can You Find FPL Points in the Chaos?</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">Mbeumo, Mainoo, Cunha or Bruno Fernandes? Which Manchester United players are worth buying in FPL for GW7, with their fixtures, minutes and value for money.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/ai-agents-playing-fantasy-premier-league"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">13 October 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">Bot user agents could be a surprisingly good way to advertise to developers</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">I built an MCP server for FPL. Then 145 user-agent strings showed up: assistants, crawlers, uptime bots, and a surprisingly effective way to advertise to developers.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/top-100-fpl-managers-gw6-transfers-and-results"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">11 October 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">The Top 100&#x27;s GW6 Bets: Newcastle Disappoints, Brighton Pays Off</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">The top 100 after GW5 averaged 67 points after hits in GW6. Their Newcastle purchases disappointed, while Brighton holdings and João Pedro captaincy paid off.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/ai-free-hit-gw6-no-haaland"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">9 October 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">I Let My FPL AI Pick a Free Hit. It Dropped Haaland.</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">I gave my FPL AI assistant £100m to pick a GW6 Free Hit. It chose Bruno captain and left out Haaland. Watch the picks and the comparison with my real team.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/use-fpl-cat-in-chatgpt-and-claude"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">8 October 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">Rate Your FPL Team With AI: Talk FPL With ChatGPT or Claude</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">ChatGPT and Claude don&#x27;t know this week&#x27;s injuries, prices or FPL rules. Connect them to FPL Cat for an AI team rating and advice on your own squad. Free.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/best-fpl-defcon-defenders"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">4 October 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">Best FPL DEFCON Defenders 2026/27: Who to Pick and Who Was Best Last Season</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">Last season&#x27;s top six FPL DEFCON defenders one year on, this season&#x27;s leaders after GW5, how possession drives DEFCON, and the defenders the FPL Cat model expects to earn the most DEFCON points in GW6–10.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/fpl-international-break-injuries"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">30 September 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">FPL Injuries: International Duty Is No Riskier Than a Gameweek</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">4 seasons of FPL data: players on international duty get hurt about as often as in a normal gameweek. Who&#x27;s injured this break: Isak, Konsa, Gakpo, Tzolis.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/fulham-fpl-team-to-watch-fixtures"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">28 September 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">Fulham: An FPL Team to Watch Before Their Two Easiest Fixtures of the Season</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">Fulham are 19th in the Premier League after five games, but our Fixture Difficulty Rating (FDR) shows their kindest run of the season starts right after the international break — three of their next six games are against the league&#x27;s only three promoted sides.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/box-to-box-midfielders-defcon-attack"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">25 September 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">FPL DEFCON Midfielders: 16 with Attacking Returns (GW1–5)</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">Which FPL midfielders combine DEFCON and attacking points? We compare 104 players with 180+ minutes; 16 earned points in both through Gameweek 5.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/how-fpl-bonus-points-work"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">24 September 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">How FPL Bonus Points Work: The BPS Explained (2026/27)</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">How Fantasy Premier League bonus points are calculated: the full 2026/27 BPS table, what changed this season, how ties are split, when bonus is confirmed, and what it took to earn bonus in Gameweeks 1-5.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/what-the-top-100-fpl-managers-did-differently"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">23 September 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">What the Top 100 FPL Managers Did Differently: The Elite Template After GW5</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">I pulled all 500 squads the top 100 Fantasy Premier League managers fielded in Gameweeks 1-5. Here&#x27;s the 15-man elite template that fits in £100m, and the players they own that you probably don&#x27;t.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/inside-the-worlds-number-1-fpl-team"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">22 September 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">Inside the World&#x27;s #1 FPL Team: Every Chip, Every Transfer, Gameweek by Gameweek</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">A data breakdown of the actual #1-ranked Fantasy Premier League manager in the world through Gameweek 5 — their real weekly scores, all four chips used in the first five gameweeks, bench points left on the table, and the squad before and after their Gameweek 4 wildcard.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/pascal-gross-should-you-buy"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">20 September 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">Should You Buy Pascal Groß in FPL? Not Yet — Here&#x27;s Why</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">In Fantasy Premier League, Pascal Groß is outscoring his underlying numbers by a wide margin this season. The points are real, but the process behind them isn&#x27;t built to last.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/welcome-to-fpl-path"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">13 September 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">Welcome to FPL Cat</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">What FPL Cat is, and how AI team analysis, dashboards, and this blog fit together.</p></a><a class="group block py-6" href="/blog/fixture-difficulty-explained"><time class="text-xs text-ink-muted">13 September 2026</time><h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-pitch-ink">Fantasy Premier League Fixture Difficulty Ratings: What They Do (and Don&#x27;t) Tell You</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">How Fantasy Premier League&#x27;s (FPL) 1-5 fixture difficulty rating works, where it&#x27;s useful, and where it misleads.</p></a></div></div></div><!--$--><!--/$--></main><footer class="border-t border-border py-6 text-center text-xs text-ink-muted"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3 justify-center"><a href="https://x.com/kotzwysp" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="X (Twitter)" class="text-ink-muted transition hover:text-ink"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" class="h-4.5 w-4.5"><path d="M13.6 10.6L20 3h-2.1l-5.3 6.1L8 3H3.3l6.6 9.6-6.9 8h2.1l5.7-6.6 5.9 6.6H21l-7.4-10.4zM11 12.2l-.7-1L5.7 4.6h2l4.2 6 .7 1 5 7.2h-2l-4.6-6.6z"></path></svg></a><a href="https://www.youtube.com/@FPLCats" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="YouTube" class="text-ink-muted transition hover:text-ink"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" class="h-4.5 w-4.5"><path d="M21.6 7.6c-.2-1-.9-1.7-1.9-2C18 5.2 12 5.2 12 5.2s-6 0-7.7.4c-1 .3-1.7 1-1.9 2C2 9.3 2 12 2 12s0 2.7.4 4.4c.2 1 .9 1.7 1.9 2 1.7.4 7.7.4 7.7.4s6 0 7.7-.4c1-.3 1.7-1 1.9-2 .4-1.7.4-4.4.4-4.4s0-2.7-.4-4.4zM10 15V9l5.2 3-5.2 3z"></path></svg></a></div><p>Data as of <!-- -->10 Nov, 18:20 UTC</p><p class="mt-1">FPL Cat is an independent project and is not affiliated with the Premier League or Fantasy Premier League.</p><p class="mt-2 flex justify-center gap-3"><a class="hover:text-ink" href="/about">About</a><a class="hover:text-ink" href="/chatgp